# @hub-lanes

# ── LANE-CPU-RANK LANE (BH-7252 C0, part of #7252) ──────────────────────────
# Daily at 14:05Z. One bin/lane-cpu-sample.sh --cpu-s window (1 h, 5 s
# interval), then the lanes ranked by CPU seconds per hour, with placement and
# hub-only reason, posted ONCE to issue lane_cpu_rank.issue (seeded 7406, code default 7252).
# After the post (state/lane-cpu-rank/state-<issue> = posted, or the marker
# comment exists) a run exits at once with no sampling.
# Off: flags/lane-off-lane-cpu-rank (bin/harness-ctl.sh off lane-cpu-rank).
5 14 * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/lane-cpu-rank.sh >> /root/harness/logs/lane-cpu-rank-cron.log 2>&1
